  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ed5c5268",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "### Summary of Loaded Tables\n",
    "\n",
    "**1. `patients`**  \n",
    "Contains 100 patients. Key variables: `gender` (categorical), `dob` (date), `expire_flag` (outcome).  \n",
    "Some date fields like `dod_hosp` and `dod_ssn` contain missing values.  \n",
    "Most columns are either numeric or textual.\n",
    "\n",
    "**2. `admissions`**  \n",
    "Includes 129 admissions. `deathtime` is essential for defining ICU mortality.  \n",
    "Text fields like `ethnicity`, `marital_status`, `language` require cleaning.  \n",
    "Several fields contain missing values.\n",
    "\n",
    "**3. `icustays`**  \n",
    "Contains 136 ICU stays.  \n",
    "`los` represents length of stay in days.  \n",
    "`intime` and `outtime` require datetime conversion.\n",
    "\n",
    "**4. `diagnoses_icd`**  \n",
    "Contains 1,761 medical diagnoses.  \n",
    "`icd9_code` is fully populated and used to detect comorbidities (e.g., CKD).\n",
    "\n",
    "**5. `d_icd_diagnoses`**  \n",
    "Maps ICD-9 codes to full descriptions (`long_title`).  \n",
    "Used to identify all CKD-related codes.\n",
    "\n",
    "**6. `outputevents`**  \n",
    "Includes 11,320 measurements such as urine output.  \n",
    "`value` contains numeric measurements, but some are missing.  \n",
    "`charttime` requires datetime conversion. Data must be filtered to ICU stays only.\n",
    "\n",
    "**7. `chartevents`**  \n",
    "Very large table (750,000+ records).  \n",
    "Only ~324,000 rows contain numeric values (`valuenum`).  \n",
    "Requires filtering and careful variable selection.\n",
    "\n",
    "**8. `d_items`**  \n",
    "Maps each `itemid` to a label, unit, and category.  \n",
    "Essential for identifying relevant measurements (e.g., Urine Output).  \n",
    "Most other fields are sparse or irrelevant."
   ]
  },
