   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "18da88ee",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Creating the Base Table for Analysis\n",
    "At this stage, we created a unified DataFrame (icu_data) that consolidates patient demographics, ICU stays, admission information, urine output, and CKD status. The merging process included:\n",
    "\n",
    "icustays (as the base) merged with:\n",
    "admissions (on subject_id, hadm_id)\n",
    "patients (on subject_id)\n",
    "CKD indicators from diagnoses_icd\n",
    "Urine output summary from outputevents\n",
    "We calculated key clinical variables:\n",
    "Age – computed from dob and ICU intime\n",
    "ICU mortality – based on whether deathtime occurred during the ICU stay\n",
    "Total urine output – summed per ICU stay\n",
    "has_ckd – binary indicator for chronic kidney disease\n",
    "This unified table will serve as the basis for exploratory data analysis (EDA) and later modeling.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "ca4a111b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "icu_data = icustays.merge(admissions, on=['subject_id', 'hadm_id'], how='left')\n",
    "\n",
    "icu_data = icu_data.merge(patients[['subject_id', 'gender', 'dob']], on='subject_id', how='left')\n",
    "\n",
    "icu_data['dob'] = pd.to_datetime(icu_data['dob'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "icu_data['intime'] = pd.to_datetime(icu_data['intime'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "icu_data['deathtime'] = pd.to_datetime(icu_data['deathtime'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "def safe_calc_age(row):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        if row['dob'] > row['intime'] or row['dob'].year > 2100:\n",
    "            return 90\n",
    "        age = (row['intime'] - row['dob']).days // 365\n",
    "        return age if 0 <= age <= 120 else 90\n",
    "    except:\n",
    "        return 90\n",
    "\n",
    "icu_data['age'] = icu_data.apply(safe_calc_age, axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "icu_data['died_in_icu'] = (\n",
    "    (icu_data['deathtime'] >= icu_data['intime']) &\n",
    "    (icu_data['deathtime'] <= icu_data['outtime'])\n",
    ").astype(int)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f689fec8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "As explained by the instructor in class, in order to preserve patient confidentiality, some elderly patients in the dataset are assigned unrealistic birth dates (e.g., over 3000 years old). These extreme values can cause issues in Pandas, particularly during date calculations, such as an \"Overflow in int64 addition\" error.\n",
    "\n",
    "To avoid this, we use a safer method to calculate age:\n",
    "Age is only computed when both dob and intime are reasonable.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both dates are explicitly converted to standard Python datetime objects using .to_pydatetime() instead of relying on Pandas’ internal datetime format.\n",
    "\n",
    "This approach ensures robust age calculation and prevents overflow errors."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3f69ccae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Adding CKD as a Comorbidity Variable\n",
    "CKD (Chronic Kidney Disease) is identified by ICD-9 codes starting with 585.\n",
    "We add a binary column has_ckd (0/1) to mark patients diagnosed with CKD, using the diagnoses_icd table.\n",
    "This variable will help assess the relationship between CKD and ICU mortality later in the analysis.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "893fac2e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "0    110\n",
      "1     26\n",
      "Name: has_ckd, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "ckd_codes = d_icd_diagnoses[\n",
    "    d_icd_diagnoses['long_title'].str.contains('chronic kidney disease', case=False, na=False)\n",
    "]['icd9_code'].unique()\n",
    "\n",
    "ckd_patients = diagnoses_icd[diagnoses_icd['icd9_code'].isin(ckd_codes)]\n",
    "\n",
    "ckd_patients = (\n",
    "    ckd_patients[['subject_id', 'hadm_id']]\n",
    "    .drop_duplicates()\n",
    "    .assign(has_ckd=1)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "icu_data = icu_data.merge(ckd_patients, on=['subject_id', 'hadm_id'], how='left')\n",
    "\n",
    "icu_data['has_ckd'] = icu_data['has_ckd'].fillna(0).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(icu_data['has_ckd'].value_counts())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "53c64943",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Adding Urine Output\n",
    "We extracted total urine output during ICU stays by:\n",
    "Identifying relevant itemids with \"urine\" in d_items.\n",
    "Filtering outputevents by these IDs and ICU timeframes.\n",
    "Summing values per ICU stay.\n",
    "Merging the result into the main dataset.\n",
    "This variable supports analysis of kidney function and mortality."
