    "# Step 3: Calculate IQR bounds\n",
    "q1 = icu_numeric['los'].quantile(0.25)\n",
    "q3 = icu_numeric['los'].quantile(0.75)\n",
    "iqr = q3 - q1\n",
    "\n",
    "lower_bound = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "upper_bound = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Lower bound: {lower_bound:.2f}, Upper bound: {upper_bound:.2f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Step 4: Identify outliers\n",
    "outliers_los = icu_numeric[\n",
    "    (icu_numeric['los'] < lower_bound) | (icu_numeric['los'] > upper_bound)\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Number of outlier rows in LOS column: {len(outliers_los)}\")\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c2f74faa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "### Summary: Outlier Analysis in Continuous Variables\n",
    "\n",
    "During this step, we analyzed three key continuous variables for outliers using the IQR method.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**1. Age**  \n",
    "- Lower bound: 43.75  \n",
    "- Upper bound: 117.75  \n",
    "- Outliers: 4 out of 136  \n",
    "- Decision: Retained. Outliers represent younger patients, and extreme ages were already handled during age calculation.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**2. Urine Output**  \n",
    "- Lower bound: 2,360  \n",
    "- Upper bound: 41,200  \n",
    "- Outliers: 54 out of 136  \n",
    "- Decision: Retained. These may reflect clinical extremes or data issues. Will be flagged and considered in later analyses.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**3. Length of Stay (LOS)**  \n",
    "- Lower bound: 3.41 days  \n",
    "- Upper bound: 8.97 days  \n",
    "- Outliers: 17 out of 136  \n",
    "- Decision: Retained. Both short and long ICU stays can have clinical relevance.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Outliers were not removed automatically. Each case was reviewed, and values were kept to preserve clinically meaningful variability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "04f9b178",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "###  Creating the \"urine_output_per_day\" Column\n",
    "\n",
    "A patient may have a high total urine output simply due to a prolonged ICU stay.\n",
    "To better evaluate kidney function, we calculate the average daily urine output by dividing the total output by the length of stay (LOS).\n",
    "This allows us to identify abnormal values relative to the duration of hospitalization rather than absolute amounts.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
